/// Get an AmigaGuide string.
///
/// This function is used to obtain a localized string given the
/// ID.
///
/// # Synopsis
///
/// txt = GetAmigaGuideString (id);
/// d0                         d0
///
/// STRPTR GetAmigaGuideString (ULONG);
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// * ID -- Valid AmigaGuide string ID, including the public `HTERR_*` error
///   constants from `libraries/amigaguide.h`.
///
/// # Returns
///
/// A pointer to the string.   NULL for an invalid string.
///
/// # Bugs
///
/// AmigaGuide 45.7 on the verified A4000 does not return for tested invalid
/// IDs `-1` and `9999`; each call remained blocked until the external 45-second
/// guest-command timeout. Pass only published IDs such as the `HTERR_*`
/// constants. A safe wrapper must reject unknown IDs before entering Tier 3.
@library("amigaguide.library")
extern pub fn GetAmigaGuideString(id: i32) -> *u8
